# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: AbiWord.
Package: AbiWord
Section: Text
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport, Iconv
Recommends: TTF-Noto-Color-Emoji
Components: Apps.Office.!AbiWord (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-gtk
Description: AbiWord word processor (GTK 3)
 The word processor: styles, tables, headers and footers, footnotes,
 lists, pictures and page layout, with OpenDocument (.odt), Word (.doc,
 .docx), RTF, HTML, text and AbiWord's own files. British English
 spelling (more dictionaries in Choices), the desktop's own fonts, RISC
 OS Save and Open boxes, Wimp menus and an icon bar icon; Word files
 open from the Filer.
 .
 This is a public beta of the riscos-gtk ports.
Build-Map: !AbiWord -> Apps/Office/!AbiWord
Build-Notice: AbiWord, packaged for PackMan from the riscos-gtk release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-gtk/releases
 .
 AbiWord is AbiWord 3.0.8 (www.abisource.com), under the GNU GPL version 2 or later, with wv (GPL). It is linked with GTK 3 and its
 libraries, enchant and hunspell (LGPL), and includes LibreOffice's
 British English dictionary (LGPL), DejaVu fonts and PThreadTicker. The
 source is offered by the Source file in the application and on the
 release page. Licences follow.
